{ 
"documentation" : "The original-indices are the two tables defining the song.  Each column in the table is a measure, and you pick one of the fragments for that measure out of the row.  Note that all the fragments in the last column are in fact identical.  You're supposed to repeat each table (song) twice.  The final column of the second repeat of the first table should be replaced with fragment 177 (the last fragment).  The indices are simply the original-indices transposed, making them easier to work with.  Each fragment has a treble and bass portion, consisting of chords of the form [note... length], where length=8 is an eighth note, length=4 is a quarter note, and so on.  Lengths for both the treble and bass sum to three quarter notes, as the song is in 3/4.",
"source" : "https://github.com/timmydoza/mozart-dice-game/",
